@startuml ICNNA_v2_0_0_packages
' ============================================================
' ICNNA v2.0.0 — Projected package diagram
' Phase 3b.2 deliverable
' ============================================================
' Log:
'   2026-04-15: FOE/Claude — File created from roadmap.
'   2026-04-20: FOE/Claude — Revised per FOE review:
'       + Added +data/+misc/ (survives; hosts spatial/ROI classes)
'       + Added +op/+pipeline (CWL/Airflow/ONNX support)
'       + Added +op/+stats (replaces erroneous +experimentSpace pkg)
'       + document class noted in +data/+core
'       + rawData importers migrate from +data/+misc to +io/+devices
'       + Lazy-proxy pattern noted (cross-cutting)
'       + Three-tier certainty: existing / planned / speculative
'       + Container packages emphasised (coloured backgrounds,
'         very thick borders)
'       + Rebranded +op/+signal as +op/+proc
'       + +qc kept: houses concrete qcCriterion subclasses
'         (abstract qc/qcCriterion stay in +data/+core)
' ============================================================
' Source: derived from Phase3_minute.tex roadmap targets,
'         Phase2c_minute.tex v2.0.0 endpoint, D.* decisions,
'         20-Apr-2026 FOE review session.
' ============================================================
' Conventions:
'   - Solid border (normal): package exists in v1.4.1-beta
'   - Solid border (bold):   <<planned>> — committed in roadmap
'   - Dashed border:         <<speculative>> — likely but not committed
'   - Container packages:    coloured bg, very thick borders
'   - All packages are <<modern>>; oo/ and +icnna.compat/ are
'     deleted by v1.8.0 / v2.0.0 respectively.
' ============================================================

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 25

' --- Tier styling via stereotypes ---
skinparam package<<planned>> {
  BorderColor DarkBlue
  BorderThickness 2
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam package<<speculative>> {
  BorderColor Gray
  BorderStyle dashed
  FontStyle italic
}
skinparam package<<container>> {
  BorderThickness 4
  FontStyle bold
}
package "src/" as src <<container>> #F0F0F0 {

  package "+icnna/" as icnna <<container>> #E8ECFF {

    package "+data" as data <<container>> #FFFDE8 {
      package "+core  (flat spine)" as core {
      }
      package "+snirf  (I/O dataset model)" as snirf
      package "+coeffs  (extinction data assets)" as coeffs
      package "+misc  (spatial, ROI, misc)" as misc
      package "+bids" <<planned>> as bids_data
      package "+synthetic" <<planned>> as synth
    }

    package "+op" as op <<container>> #E8FFE8 {
      package "+snirf" as op_snirf
      package "+proc" <<planned>> as op_proc {
        package "+motion" <<planned>> as op_motion
        package "+physio" <<planned>> as op_physio
      }
      package "+bids" <<planned>> as op_bids
      package "+experiment" <<planned>> as op_exp
      package "+pipeline" <<planned>> as op_pipeline
      package "+stats" <<planned>> as op_stats
    }

    package "+analysis" <<planned>> as analysis
    package "+qc" <<planned>> as qc
    package "+registration" <<planned>> as reg

    package "+io" as io <<container>> #FFE8E0 {
      package "+snirf" as io_snirf
      package "+bids" <<planned>> as io_bids
      package "+devices" <<planned>> as io_devices
      package "+legacy_mat" <<planned>> as io_matload
    }

    package "+plot" as plot
    package "+util" as util

    package "+gui" <<planned>> as guipkg {
      package "+model" <<planned>>
      package "+view" <<planned>>
      package "+controller" <<planned>>
    }
  }

  ' compat removed at v2.0.0 — show as ghost for traceability
  package "+icnna.compat/  <<deleted at v2.0.0>>" as compat #LightGray
}

' --- Dependencies (intra-modern, flat-architecture) ---
op        --> core       : "operates over"
op_proc   --> core
op_motion --> op_proc
op_physio --> op_proc
op_exp    --> core
op_snirf  --> snirf
op_snirf  --> core
op_bids   --> bids_data
op_bids   --> core
op_pipeline --> core     : "sequences ops\nover core data"
op_pipeline --> op_proc
op_stats  --> core       : "statistical ops\n(distances, embeddings,\nclustering)"
op_stats  --> analysis

io_snirf  --> snirf
io_bids   --> bids_data
io_devices --> core      : "device importers\n(rawData_NIRx etc.)"
io_matload --> core      : "loads legacy .mat\ninto modern spine"

analysis  --> core
qc        --> core       : "concrete qcCriterion\nsubclasses"
qc        --> op_proc
reg       --> core

plot      --> core
plot      --> analysis
plot      --> qc

guipkg    --> core       : "model layer"
guipkg    --> op
guipkg    --> analysis
guipkg    --> qc
guipkg    --> reg
guipkg    --> io
guipkg    --> plot

synth     --> core       : "produces synthetic\nbundles for QC/op tests"
misc      --> core

' ================================================================
' NOTES
' ================================================================

note bottom of compat
  +icnna.compat/ existed v1.4.3.x -> v1.7.x for
  bridging legacy <-> modern call sites.
  Deleted at v2.0.0 per Phase 3 Rule 5.
  Shown ghosted for historical traceability only.
end note

note bottom of guipkg
  Unified GUI subsumes legacy GUI/ entry points
  including the registration tool. MVC split is
  the architectural commitment from v1.9.0.
end note

note right of io_matload
  N.6 -- .mat load-compat adapters retained
  past +icnna.compat removal; final deletion v2.0.0.
end note

note bottom of io_devices
  Device-specific importers migrated here
  from +data/+misc/ (e.g. rawData_NIRx)
  and from oo/ legacy rawData_* classes.
  Each importer subclasses +data/+core/rawData.
end note

note right of op_pipeline
  Pipeline representation and execution.
  Standard support planned:
  CWL, Apache Airflow DAG, ONNX.
  See overprocessing & pipeline
  optimization papers.
end note

note bottom of op_stats
  Statistical operations on experimentBundles:
  distance metrics, embeddings (MDS etc.),
  clustering. Replaces legacy analysis/
  experimentSpace computational behaviour.
  Domain class experimentBundle stays in +core.
end note

note bottom of qc
  Houses concrete qcCriterion subclasses:
  _Saturation, _Mirroring, _ChannelIntegrity
  (v1.5.4 survival tier);
  _SCI, _CV (v1.6.4 enhancement tier).
  Abstract qc/qcCriterion contracts remain
  in +data/+core.
end note

note bottom of core
  Key v2.0.0 additions to +core:
  ..
  **document** (<<speculative>>)
    Top-level container; holds experiment(s).
    v2.0.0: single-experiment.
    Post-v2.0.0: multi-experiment (meta-analysis).
  ..
  **experiment** (<<planned>>)
    Modern replacement for legacy experiment.
    Mediates group <-> unit associations.
    Manages design (via experimentDesign),
    sessions, devices, and bundles.
  ..
  **session** (<<planned>>)
    Modern replacement for legacy session.
    Holds devices, runs, timeline.
    sessionDefinition (<<speculative>>)
    provides the template/contract.
  ..
  **run** (<<speculative>>)
    Temporal subdivision of a session
    (from Cantor hub_run).
  ..
  **experimentDesign** (<<speculative>>)
    Experimental design taxonomy (extracted
    from experiment.designType struct).
  ..
  **Lazy-proxy pattern** (<<planned>>, cross-cutting)
    Data containers load arrays on demand,
    not at construction time. Enables large
    datasets without exhausting memory.
end note

note bottom of misc
  Hosts modern equivalents of spatial/ROI
  classes (imagePartition, roi, menaGrid, etc.).
  Exact class list is speculative; created as
  legacy classes are migrated.
end note

' ================================================================
' LEGEND
' ================================================================
legend bottom left
  |= Border |= Meaning |
  | <size:12>----</size> solid, normal | Exists in v1.4.1-beta |
  | <size:12><b>====</b></size> solid, bold+blue | <<planned>> -- committed in roadmap |
  | <size:12>- - -</size> dashed, gray | <<speculative>> -- likely but not committed |
  | <size:12><b>####</b></size> thick, dark | <<container>> -- grouping package |
  ..
  Milestone versions shown where known.
  All oo/ classes deleted at v1.8.0.
  .mat load-compat adapters removed at v2.0.0.
end legend

@enduml
